the overwhelming majority of prehensile  tails in nature are round but seahorse  tails are square so what does having a  square tail do for the seahorse to find  out  researchers printed a 3d model of a  segment of the seahorses square tail  structure complete with vertebrae and  outer skeleton and they pitted it  against a model of a hypothetical round  tail hypothetical since round seahorse  tails don't exist in nature they hit the  models with a mallet simulating the  crushing jaws of a water bird the square  tail came out the clear winner its  smoothly overlapping joints made it  strong and resilient absorbing more  energy upon impact than the circular  tail the researchers also simulated the  seahorses prehensile grasp the square  model maintained a better grip because  it shared more surface area with the  object it was holding on to future  seahorse inspired inventions could  include a flexible robotic arm for  performing surgery rescue and  exploration robots that fit into tight  spaces and flexible lightweight body  armor with or without a tail  you
 

